<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meena</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Meena, also written Mina, are a community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> and neighbouring regions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and one of the state's largest scheduled tribes. Tradition holds that Meena chiefs ruled parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a> region, including Amber, before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachhwaha Rajputs</a> took it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>. Under British rule they were classed as a 'criminal tribe', and since independence many have become prominent in public life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meena.jpg" alt="Meena" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Frith · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EMuseumPlus_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
